  "body": "`RESEND_API_KEY` was sitting in `.env` with nothing reading it \u2014 the defect #110 fixed for three other secrets. This adds the one thing that proves a credential: a command that runs.\n\n## What this adds\n\n| file | owns |\n|---|---|\n| `ingest/notify/resend_api.py` | `send()` \u2014 one authenticated JSON POST, `permit()` before the socket, raises on every non-2xx carrying Resend's own sentence |\n| `serve/commands/run_email.py` | `quantamind email --to ...`; exit 2 naming `RESEND_API_KEY` when unset |\n| `types/deployment.py` | `Destination.NOTIFICATIONS` \u2014 air-gapped refuses mail by name |\n| `serve/arguments.py` | `build_parser` and `UNBUILT`, split out of `cli.py` |\n\n**No `resend` SDK.** `pyproject.toml` declares `dependencies = []`, and this needs a JSON POST with a bearer token \u2014 the same argument `ingest/payments/stripe_api.py` makes against Stripe's SDK. The cost is paid explicitly: `tests/unit/layers/ingest/test_resend_request.py` checks the body, because nothing else does.\n\n**The key is never on `Settings`.** `quantamind config` prints that object. It is read at the command through `types/dotenv.credential`, beside the Stripe key, and passed down.\n\n**On-prem permits mail and air-gapped does not**, which is a decision and the weaker case than `PAYMENTS`: mail leaves through a third party rather than through the customer's own GitHub, so an operator who considers that egress unacceptable runs the air-gapped shape rather than finding the attempt in their logs.\n\n## The CLI split, and the guard it silently inverted\n\n`serve/cli.py` sat at **exactly** the 200-line cap, so `email` could not be added to it. `build_parser` and `UNBUILT` moved to `serve/arguments.py`, re-exported from `cli.py`.\n\n`records/declared_commands.py` reads `add_parser` calls out of the AST of one named file. After the move that file held none, so all 30 documented commands were reported unregistered \u2014 against prose nobody had touched.\n\n**It failed loudly only by luck.** The same function returned two empty sets when the path did not exist at all, and an empty set of registered commands makes every \"is this documented\" check pass by having no subject \u2014 a flood and a silence, neither saying *the guard lost its subject*. That fallback is now `ParserMoved`, raised by name, with a known-answer test in `test_documented_recipes_spans.py`. The fixture there now takes the path from the guard instead of restating it, which is the only reason it broke at all.\n\n## Sabotage found a gap in my own tests\n\nDeleting `permit(...)` from `send` left **every new test green**. They assert the permission *table*, not that anything consults it. Only `check_network_chokepoint.py` caught it \u2014 and a promise with one mechanism behind it is the shape rule 7 already shipped broken here.\n\n`test_send_itself_refuses_under_air_gapped_and_never_opens_a_socket` closes it. Re-running the sabotage now fails without the guard's help. Two other sabotages (filtering a blank recipient instead of refusing; letting air-gapped reach notifications) were caught by tests as written.\n\n## Verified by running it, not by reading it\n\n- Two live messages accepted by Resend: `01a0baa1-3c15-705e-a65f-005911116976`, `01a0bab3-0771-731b-80b9-c99a7494aecd`\n- `QUANTAMIND_DEPLOYMENT_SHAPE=air_gapped` \u2192 *\"air_gapped deployment refuses notifications ... Nothing was sent.\"*, exit 2\n- Unset key \u2192 names `RESEND_API_KEY`, exit 2\n- `just check` green, `just verify` green (50 live tests, 3m50s)\n\n## What could still silently fail\n\n**`onboarding@resend.dev` delivers only to the Resend account owner.** Mail from it to any other address is accepted and never arrives \u2014 accepted-but-undelivered looks exactly like success. This is why `run_email` prints the id and states that acceptance is not delivery rather than printing \"sent\". Mailing anyone else needs `--from` on a domain verified in the account.\n\n**A 2xx means queued**, not received. The inbox is an event this process never observes, so the id is the only handle and the command says so.\n\n**Nothing calls this except a person typing it.** If a future caller sends mail automatically, the decision about when belongs at that caller \u2014 the argument `ingest/publish/__init__.py` makes about `POSTING_ENABLED`: grouping does not gate.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nSix of seven. **Item 7 \u2014 a second reviewer running `just verify` locally \u2014 has not happened**; this was written and verified in one session by one person.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
